{
  "@context": {
    "@vocab": "https://danbri.github.io/glitchcan-minigam/inklet/finkapp/apps/vocab#"
  },
  "@id": "podnotes",
  "@type": "App",
  "position": 32,
  "id": "podnotes",
  "family": "office",
  "icon": "🗒️",
  "name": "Notes",
  "surface": "window",
  "url": "../apps/podnotes/index.html",
  "desc": "Plain notes, kept in your pod",
  "capabilities": [
    "pod:read",
    "pod:write"
  ],
  "silent": true,
  "tools": true,
  "handles": [
    {
      "types": [
        "text/plain",
        "text/markdown"
      ],
      "extensions": [
        "txt",
        "md",
        "text"
      ],
      "actions": [
        "view",
        "edit"
      ],
      "comment": "A plain text editor. Markdown opens as its source, with no preview. Pod verbs carry at most 1 MiB, so very large logs will not open."
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "TOOLS (2026-11-07): list_notes and read_note (read-only) and add_note (writes, so an outside caller needs a grant), through foafos.tools in app-sdk.js.",
    "The first caller of the pod verbs (foafos.pod.get/list/put/delete in inklet/apps/app-sdk.js). It reaches only apps/podnotes/ in the pod the person marked \"apps use this\" in System's Pods tab, and never sees the pod's address or password. Saves send the ETag it read, so a note changed elsewhere is not overwritten.",
    "handles: exploring, and may change. docs/foafos-open-with-20261105.md.",
    "Beyond its own container, a window can hold one file the shell shared with it."
  ]
}
